<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raghunatha Nayak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1600">1600</a>–1634</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raghunatha <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayaka">Nayak</a> was the most celebrated ruler of the Nayak kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> in the Kaveri delta. A loyal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a>, he fought for it in its succession war, notably at Toppur in 1616. A poet and musician, he made his court a centre of Telugu literature and Carnatic music.</p></div>
